#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:1
msgid "Class: RoundRobinPool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:3
msgid "Extends: `undici.Dispatcher`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:5
msgid ""
"A pool of [Client](/docs/docs/api/Client.md) instances connected to the "
"same upstream target with round-robin client selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:7
msgid ""
"Unlike [`Pool`](/docs/docs/api/Pool.md), which always selects the first "
"available client, `RoundRobinPool` cycles through clients in a round-"
"robin fashion. This ensures even distribution of requests across all "
"connections, which is particularly useful when the upstream target is "
"behind a load balancer that round-robins TCP connections across multiple "
"backend servers (e.g., Kubernetes Services)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:9
msgid "Requests are not guaranteed to be dispatched in order of invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:11
msgid "`new RoundRobinPool(url[, options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:13
msgid "Arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:15
msgid ""
"**url** `URL | string` - It should only include the **protocol, hostname,"
" and port**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:16
msgid "**options** `RoundRobinPoolOptions` (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:18
msgid "Parameter: `RoundRobinPoolOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:20
msgid ""
"Extends: [`ClientOptions`](/docs/docs/api/Client.md#parameter-"
"clientoptions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:22
msgid ""
"**factory** `(origin: URL, opts: Object) => Dispatcher` - Default: "
"`(origin, opts) => new Client(origin, opts)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:23
msgid ""
"**connections** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `null` - The number"
" of `Client` instances to create. When set to `null`, the "
"`RoundRobinPool` instance will create an unlimited amount of `Client` "
"instances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:24
msgid ""
"**clientTtl** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `null` - The amount "
"of time before a `Client` instance is removed from the `RoundRobinPool` "
"and closed. When set to `null`, `Client` instances will not be removed or"
" closed based on age."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:26
msgid "Use Case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:28
msgid "`RoundRobinPool` is designed for scenarios where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:30
msgid "You connect to a single origin (e.g., `http://my-service.namespace.svc`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:31
msgid ""
"That origin is backed by a load balancer distributing TCP connections "
"across multiple servers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:32
msgid "You want requests evenly distributed across all backend servers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:34
msgid ""
"**Example**: In Kubernetes, when using a Service DNS name with multiple "
"Pod replicas, kube-proxy load balances TCP connections. `RoundRobinPool` "
"ensures each connection (and thus each Pod) receives an equal share of "
"requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:36
msgid "Important: Backend Distribution Considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:38
msgid ""
"`RoundRobinPool` distributes **HTTP requests** evenly across **TCP "
"connections**. Whether this translates to even backend server "
"distribution depends on the load balancer's behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:40
msgid "**✓ Works when the load balancer**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:41
msgid ""
"Assigns different backends to different TCP connections from the same "
"client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:42
msgid ""
"Uses algorithms like: round-robin, random, least-connections (without "
"client affinity)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:43
msgid "Example: Default Kubernetes Services without `sessionAffinity`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:45
msgid "**✗ Does NOT work when**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:46
msgid ""
"Load balancer has client/source IP affinity (all connections from one IP "
"→ same backend)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:47
msgid "Load balancer uses source-IP-hash or sticky sessions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:49
msgid "**How it works:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:50
msgid "`RoundRobinPool` creates N TCP connections to the load balancer endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:51
msgid "Load balancer assigns each TCP connection to a backend (per its algorithm)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:52
msgid "`RoundRobinPool` cycles HTTP requests across those N connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:53
msgid ""
"Result: Requests distributed proportionally to how the LB distributed the"
" connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RoundRobinPool.md:55
msgid ""
"If the load balancer assigns all connections to the same backend (e.g., "
"due to session affinity), `RoundRobinPool` cannot overcome this. In such "
"cases, consider using [`BalancedPool`](/docs/docs/api/BalancedPool.md) "
"with direct backend addresses (e.g., individual pod IPs) instead of a "
"load-balanced endpoint."
msgstr ""

